Short:        MSX/MSX2/MSX2+ emulator, accuracy update
Author:       Juan Antonio Gomez Galvez (RED Soft); 4.0 changes: <uploader>
Uploader:     <uploader> (<email>)
Type:         misc/emu
Version:      4.0
Replaces:     -
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     68030 or better (68020 runs with the A1200 preset), AGA or ECS
Distribution: Aminet
Kurz:         MSX/MSX2/MSX2+ Emulator, Genauigkeits-Update

DRAFT - not for upload until the original author agrees to the release,
its name and its licence (see Docs/release_4.0.md).

AmiMSX 4.0 is an update of AmiMSX 3.1 by Juan Antonio Gomez Galvez
(RED Soft), built from the 3.1 source released on Aminet
(misc/emu/AmiMSX_asm). This version puts accuracy first: a fast 68030 or
68040 is the baseline, and PiStorm (Emu68) systems have speed to spare.

What's new
----------
- Sprite collisions (S#0), the 5th sprite flag and mid-frame splits
  (sprite tables, SCREEN 4 tables, SCREEN 5/4 modes, palettes, R#8/R#18/R#23).
- Z80 fixes: POP/RET through ROM, NEG/CPL flags, M1 wait states, LD A,R.
- VDP command fixes: transparent copies, LMMC.
- 48/64 KB linear ROMs, 4 MB ROMs, openMSX-style mapper guessing.
- Three Workbench presets (A1200, 030, PiStorm) using the new
  PREFS=<file> ToolType.
- Ships with C-BIOS 0.29 as AmiMSX2.data. See below for disks and BASIC.

See CHANGES_4.0 for the full list.

System ROMs
-----------
The included AmiMSX2.data holds C-BIOS (http://cbios.sourceforge.net), a
free MSX BIOS that runs cartridges. It has no MSX-BASIC and no disk ROM.
For disk images (MVD) and BASIC, copy AmiMSX2.data from the AmiMSX 3.2
package (Aminet misc/emu/AmiMSX) over the included one.

Installation
------------
Copy the AmiMSX drawer anywhere. Start one of the preset icons:
  AmiMSX A1200    68020/14 MHz: sprites every 2nd frame, no collisions
  AmiMSX 030      68030/50 MHz: sprites every frame, collisions on
  AmiMSX PiStorm  Emu68: everything at full accuracy
Each preset keeps its own settings file. Save Prefs in the menu writes to
the preset you started.

